=== Phase G: marketplace evidence ===
date: 2026-08-12T03:35:20Z

## RESULT: FAIL (release-blocking schema/type mismatch)

## Finding
enterprise_marketplace_assets + enterprise_marketplace_asset_snapshots ID/FK columns
were created as VARCHAR(36) by B4 migration
(api/migrations/versions/2026_07_21_1400-b416e5c4e702..., sa.String(length=36)),
but the ORM model (api/models/model.py) declares them as StringUUID, which maps to
PostgreSQL UUID type. Runtime queries that filter on these columns bind UUID params,
and PostgreSQL rejects them against varchar columns:
  psycopg2.errors.UndefinedFunction: operator does not exist: character varying = uuid

## Blast radius (all fail with 500 unknown)
- POST /apps/{id}/enterprise-marketplace/submissions  -> 500 (filters source_app_id)
- GET  /enterprise-marketplace/submissions           -> 500 (filters source_tenant_id)
- GET  /enterprise-marketplace/assets/{id}           -> 500 (filters id)
- POST /enterprise-marketplace/assets/{id}/copies    -> 500 (filters id)
- POST /platform-admin/.../{id}/reviews              -> 500 (filters id)
- POST /platform-admin/.../{id}/unlist               -> 500 (filters id)

## Working
- GET  /enterprise-marketplace/assets                -> 200 (filters publication_status only)
- GET  /platform-admin/enterprise-marketplace/assets -> 200 (admin list, items=1)

## DB column types (isolated primary DB, POST-upgrade)
accounts.id          = uuid
apps.id              = uuid
datasets.id          = uuid
enterprise_marketplace_assets.id / source_app_id / source_tenant_id / submitter_account_id = varchar  <- MISMATCH
enterprise_marketplace_asset_snapshots.id / asset_id / source_app_id / source_tenant_id / submitter_account_id = varchar  <- MISMATCH

## Root cause location (read-only reference)
model: api/models/model.py:2847-2848 EnterpriseMarketplaceAsset.source_tenant_id/source_app_id StringUUID
migration: api/migrations/versions/2026_07_21_1400-b416e5c4e702... lines 60-71 sa.String(length=36)

## Impact
Entire marketplace lifecycle (submit->review->copy->unlist) unusable on PostgreSQL.
Affects both upgraded production copy AND fresh installs (same migration path).
Blocks release: VALIDATION_PLAN marketplace scenarios cannot pass.

## Deviation from plan
Marketplace scenarios executed but FAIL; root cause is a real schema bug, not an env issue.
